# Where `trigger.dev deploy` writes the bundle and the generated Containerfile. Ignored for a
# stronger reason than noise: on a REAL deploy the build manifest's `deploy.env` is seeded from the
# project's server-side environment variables as VALUES, not names, so a committed build directory
# would commit Production's credentials. (On `--dry-run` it was observed empty — 2026-09-14,
# during development — but that is the CLI's choice, not a guarantee to rely on.)
.trigger/

# packages/app/src/boundary.test.ts plants this module in `src` for one case and removes it again.
# Ignored so a run killed mid-case cannot leave a committable file behind.
packages/app/src/planted-by-boundary-test.ts

# packages/cli/src/init-boundary.test.ts does the same, for the rule that keeps the registration
# secrets off every surface.
packages/cli/src/planted-by-init-boundary-test.ts
